WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.009
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.080
I am sure that every one of us have overheard
conversations at a workplace where people

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:16.670
talked about taking the stairs instead of
the elevator, and, as a result, getting leaner.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:21.730
There was also a running joke on the internet
about Arnold Classic, a famous bodybuilding

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:28.770
competition/festival, where I think it's fair
to say that people tended to favor the escalator

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:35.830
instead of the stairs. So, this is it, we're
going to settle this here and now. Do we get

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:39.370
lean from taking the stairs every day?

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:45.110
Scientists set up a controlled experiment
where over a hundred subjects climbed 11 stories

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:52.079
of staircases, ascending a total of 27 meters
vertically. Their oxygen consumption and heart

00:00:52.079 --> 00:00:57.840
rate was measured, and most importantly for
us, the amount of caloric cost of this undertaking.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:05.289
They have found that all this self flagellation
with ascending 11 stories of staircases burns

00:01:05.289 --> 00:01:14.200
a whopping 19.7 kilo calories. Each step is
worth approximately one tenth of a kilo calorie

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:20.759
if we're ascending. Descending is worth approximately
half of that. Apparently, these bodybuilders

00:01:20.759 --> 00:01:22.509
know what they are doing.

00:01:22.509 --> 00:01:28.100
The authors diplomatically noted:
Stair-climbing exercise using a local public-access

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:33.310
staircase met the minimum requirements for
cardiorespiratory benefits and can therefore

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:39.829
be considered a viable exercise for most people
and suitable for promotion of physical activity.

00:01:39.829 --> 00:01:45.579
Which sounds like the scientific equivalent
of "well, better than nothing".

00:01:45.579 --> 00:01:49.979
So does this mean that you shouldn't take
the stairs at work? If you're looking to get

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:56.740
lean because of that, no, not a chance. However,
if you are looking for a refreshing cardiovascular

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:02.169
exercise in the morning that refreshes your
body, and makes you happier, start climbing.

00:02:02.169 --> 00:02:05.240
I do it all the time and I love it!

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:11.200
So, we are exploring so far uncharted territories
and this makes the first episode on nutrition

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.730
(should have said exercise, sorry!) in the
series, if you would like to hear more of

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:18.810
this, let me know in the comments section.
I'd also be happy to see your paper recommendations

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.480
in nutrition as well.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:24.040
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

